  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `crates/app/src/operation/kept_rejudge.rs`: the post's live re-judge of kept parts (#1628) now uses the same law split as generation (`generate::run_job_arms`):\n  - a stock-source Engrave or Trace: the mark law (no change);\n  - a stock-source Drill, Bore or Thread: the containment law. The declared holes' modelled walls are excused (#1631). The thread grant is read as generation reads it. If the re-judge cannot read it, it gives no grant (the stricter law).\n  - a stock-source cross drill: the radial law `cross_part::part_clear` (#1635);\n  - all other kinds, and the neighbours of a part source: the plain solid law (no change). A part-source cross drill also answers to `cross_part::neighbours_clear` (#1641), as at generation.\n- `crates/app/tests/stock_source_holes.rs`: a new pinning test.\n- `docs/decisions/1691-live-judge-hole-excuse.md`: the decision.\n\n## Cause\n\nConfirmed on `4f4edcf35`. The refusal text \"S1 now cuts part ...\" comes from `kept_rejudge::moved_part_problem`. That function judged every kept part with `DepthLaw::Keep` and no excused walls. The faceted wall of a modelled hole then counts as a cut. Generation does not convict the same path.\n\n## How tested\n\n- `stock_source_cross_drill`: 6 passed (failed 1 on `4f4edcf35`).\n- `stock_source_holes`: 7 passed (failed 1 on `4f4edcf35`, plus the new test).\n- `kept_parts_live`: 4 passed. `stock_source_law`: 7 passed. `cross_drill_neighbours`: 5 passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests --lib -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Pinning test: `a_part_added_under_a_stock_source_drill_is_judged_at_the_post_by_the_hole_law`. On a turned stock, a part is added under a clean stock-source drill. With a modelled hole there, the program posts. Solid there, the post refuses with \"S1 now cuts part 'other'\".\n- The guard was seen to fail: with the hole law removed from the re-judge, the solid case posted (a `G81` into the part), and the test failed. With the guard, it passes.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The full quick and batch gates (targeted suites only, as asked).\n- A 3+2 (tilted frame) stock-source hole or cross drill at the post.\n- A stock-source Thread on a turned stock: generation refuses it before the post.\n\nChangelog: The post no longer refuses a legal stock-source drill, bore, thread or cross drill in the part's own modelled hole on a turned stock (#1691).\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #1691\n",
